Do it exactly like this in Terminal.
1) Go to lab1-hello-world and pull latest version
cd ~/lab1-hello-world
git pull
If it says No such file or directory, try:
cd ~/Desktop/lab1-hello-world
git pull
2) Go to your lab4 project
cd ~/lab4-word-game
If it says No such file or directory, try:
cd ~/Desktop/lab4-word-game
3) Delete your old local .github folder
rm -rf .github
4) Delete journal/instructions files from the root folder
Run this inside lab4-word-game:
rm -f JOURNAL.md REPORT.md MY_NOTES.md copilot-instructions.md ai4se.instructions.md
Do not delete README.md unless your teacher told you to.
5) Copy .github from lab1-hello-world into lab4
Try this first:
cp -R ~/lab1-hello-world/.github .
If that gives an error, use:
cp -R ~/Desktop/lab1-hello-world/.github .
6) Check it worked
ls -la
ls -la .github
You should see a .github folder.
7) Push everything to GitHub
git status
git add .
git commit -m "Update github instructions and journal setup"
git push
If it says nothing to commit, that’s okay. Just do:
git status






